   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let p(x) = ln(x + 3) / (x^2 - 7x + 10). Consider the largest interval that contains x = 0 and on which p is continuous. What is the sum of the integers in that interval?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "numeric",
      "mathjson": -2
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The logarithm requires x + 3 > 0, so x > -3, and the denominator x^2 - 7x + 10 = (x - 2)(x - 5) is zero at x = 2 and x = 5, so those inputs are excluded too.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Subtract",
               "x",
               2
            ],
            [
               "Subtract",
               "x",
               5
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "p is a quotient of a logarithmic function and a polynomial, each continuous on its domain, so p is continuous on (-3, 2) U (2, 5) U (5, infinity).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Ln",
               [
                  "Add",
                  "x",
                  3
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Multiply",
               [
                  "Subtract",
                  "x",
                  2
               ],
               [
                  "Subtract",
                  "x",
                  5
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The piece that contains x = 0 is (-3, 2), open at -3 because ln 0 is undefined and open at 2 because the denominator is zero. Its integers are -2, -1, 0 and 1.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            -2,
            -1,
            0,
            1
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The sum of those integers is -2.",
         "mathjson": -2
      }
   ],
